  "mechanism_c_verdict": "The τ-functor DOES structurally dictate a real projection, but NOT Re(Li_2^q). Two distinct archimedean rules apply: (1) on the MULTIPLICATIVE quantum-volume generator (T1=∏V̂_i) the rule is τ_arch=ln|·|_∞ (def:algebraic-quantum-volume) — T1 is already real. (2) on the dilogarithm/brane-tower object (T2,T3) the archimedean image is the BLOCH-WIGNER dilogarithm D(z)=Im Li_2+log|z|·arg(1−z) (prop:vol-through-tau, archimedean-functor-uniqueness, Bloch-Suslin), which is REAL BY CONSTRUCTION. Taking Re(Li_2^q) is NOT what the functor says; the functor says take the Bloch-Wigner combination. DERIVED-real IFF the production tower equals the Bloch-Wigner image; CHOSEN-real if one simply drops Im.",
