  "mechanism_a_verdict": "Im does NOT cancel within a single particle. The proton tower Im = 0.656782371738 (nonzero). Each generator with |V̂_i|>q₀ contributes a same-sign Im (the +i0 branch fixes the sign), and they ADD. Mechanism (a) REFUTED structurally — there is no cancellation, so this is a clean negative, not a chosen projection.",
  "mechanism_b_verdict": "The electron figure-8 tower is REAL (Im=0.0); the proton/electron ratio is STILL COMPLEX. Im does NOT cancel in the normalisation ratio: proton and electron towers have independent, unequal imaginary parts that do not divide out. Mechanism (b) REFUTED.",
  "VERDICT": "The naive Re(Li_2^q) projection is CHOSEN-real (dropping Im because 'mass must be real' is a fit). The branch-average is CHOSEN-real (equals Re by construction, not the canonical +i0 branch). Im does NOT cancel across generators (mech a) nor through the m_e normalisation ratio (mech b). The ONLY structurally-DERIVED real projection is the BLOCH-WIGNER dilogarithm D(z)=Im Li_2+log|z|·arg(1−z) dictated by prop:vol-through-tau / archimedean-functor-uniqueness (Bloch-Suslin pentagon-uniqueness) — BUT that requires the production brane-tower object to literally BE the archimedean image of a pentagon-coherent Bloch-group class, i.e. T2/T3 = Σ D, a DIFFERENT functional from Re(Li_2^q). See the audit doc for the DERIVED-vs-CHOSEN classification and the raw m_p per projection. The continued tower CONVERGES but its archimedean reality is DERIVED only through the Bloch-Wigner route, not by taking Re — a genuine structural distinction, not a free real projection.",
